  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    The Ofundis∴flux was a catastrophic eruption of aurora-fire through the deep tunnels beneath Sleek☽ Caemomot, a major Nightshelf mining settlement, during the Frozen Peace. The ice fractured without warning, releasing upward columns of light intense enough to blind miners for days and flooding fissures with molten aurora-fire — a phenomenon that should not occur naturally at mining depth. Cavern walls crystallized into material of extraordinary hardness and density.
    
    Three mining crews were underground when the event began. The miner Keelo, working the eastern vein, carried her apprentice ☽'viat to the surface despite severe burns to her flippers. She returned for the remaining crews and did not emerge. Her body has not been recovered.
    
    ## Consequences
    
    The crystallization produced **The Thrumed~ Shadow-glass**, an artifact of anomalous density that resonates audibly when struck. Five separate Nightshelf laws and memorials were enacted in response: **Echo∴eliquiae**, **Foedus∴vincu**, **Mandatum∴ccord**, **Memoria∴moria**, and **Ritus∴um** — an extraordinary legislative response that speaks to the event's severity more precisely than casualty figures the records do not preserve.
    
    The Ofundis∴flux also further damaged **The Radiant Ring**, an aurora-glass war hammer carried by the warrior ☽'Netemia, widening existing fractures in the weapon's head. The event is additionally credited as the catalyst for **Fissure☽ Aurora**, the Nightshelf technique of fracturing aurora-light into usable fire — a practice whose origins in disaster are worth remembering when evaluating its continued use.
